{
  "total": 55.72,
  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "show": "On this day in 1869, two men tried to corner America's gold.",
      "start": 0.4,
      "end": 5.925
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "show": "Jay Gould and his partner, James Fisk, had a plan. Buy up the gold, and force the price up on the New York Gold Exchange.",
      "start": 6.475,
      "end": 15.499
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "show": "There was one problem. Every two weeks, the Treasury sold gold of its own.",
      "start": 15.999,
      "end": 21.055
    },
    {
      "id": "s4a",
      "show": "So they found a way in.",
      "start": 21.605,
      "end": 23.312
    },
    {
      "id": "s4b",
      "show": "Their inside man?",
      "start": 23.662,
      "end": 25.134
    },
    {
      "id": "s4c",
      "show": "The President's own brother-in-law.",
      "start": 25.584,
      "end": 27.781
    },
    {
      "id": "s5a",
      "show": "But on Friday, 24 September, President Grant ordered the Treasury to sell.",
      "start": 28.281,
      "end": 34.084
    },
    {
      "id": "s5b",
      "show": "And the price collapsed. From 162½, to 133.",
      "start": 34.384,
      "end": 39.248
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "show": "They called it Black Friday.",
      "start": 39.848,
      "end": 41.619
    },
    {
      "id": "s7a",
      "show": "And James Fisk?",
      "start": 42.369,
      "end": 43.862
    },
    {
      "id": "s7b",
      "show": "Less than three years later, he was assassinated in New York.",
      "start": 44.262,
      "end": 48.358
    },
    {
      "id": "s8a",
      "show": "Every day has a story like this.",
      "start": 49.158,
      "end": 51.526
    },
    {
      "id": "s8b",
      "show": "History Unlocked.",
      "start": 51.876,
      "end": 53.455
    },
    {
      "id": "s8c",
      "show": "Link in bio.",
      "start": 53.755,
      "end": 55.12
    }
  ]
